## Summary

I implemented the native **SwiftUI `SharedDrivePage`** at full web parity with `web/src/features/sharing/pages/SharedDrivePage.tsx` (public route `/s/:token`), covering all **43 parity items** (11 panels + 4 charts + 5 maps + 3 states + 20 strings).

**Delivered** (`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Sharing/`, 10 files + 1 test, 1642 LOC vs 455 web):
- **Model layer** — pure-Foundation SI value types + a `SharedDriveWire` v1/v2 normalizer (ports web `normalizeSharedDriveData`), a `@MainActor @Observable SharedDrivePageModel` (ADR-004, no networking in view) with a `SharedDriveDataSource` seam and loading/ready/expired phases.
- **View layer** — branded header, hero MapKit route map (polyline + green-start/red-end circle markers + style switcher via P3 `TSMapView`), title/date/endpoints, the 7-tile adaptive stat grid, vehicle `GlassPanel`, elevation (`TSAreaChart`) + speed (`TSLineChart`) Swift-Charts profiles, the no-map-data empty panel, footer, and the expired view — SI-in/display-out via the shared `Units` engine, adaptive macOS+iOS.
- **Navigation** — typed `SharedDriveLink` destination + SwiftUI-free `SharedDriveDeepLink` `/s/:token` parser (sibling TripReplay/DriveDetail precedent).
- **20 `share.*` keys** added verbatim to `Localizable.xcstrings`; **+2 ledger rows** (43/43); evidence log.

**Verification (all green):** xcodegen `0`, swiftformat `--lint` `0/11`, scoped swiftlint `--strict` `0/11`, placeholder scan `0`, an **executed 31/31 logic harness**, and strict-concurrency isolated type-checks on **macOS + iOS (0/0)**.

Notably, the strict-concurrency type-check **caught and I fixed a real Swift-6 bug** — `static let LocalizedStringKey` is a non-Sendable global under the project's `SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY: complete`, which would have broken the real build; switched to computed `static var`s. The full `xcodebuild` is deferred (the KMP `Shared.xcframework` isn't staged — out-of-scope infra, identical to every sibling P7 page). Committed as `15571098c`.



